          "settings": {
            "title": "What is the difference between porcelain tiles and ceramic tiles?",
            "answer": "<p>Porcelain tiles are denser, less porous, and fired at higher temperatures than ceramic tiles. This makes porcelain tiles more durable, water-resistant, and suitable for both wall and floor use in bathrooms, kitchens, and living areas.</p>"
